<BaseLayout
	title="How this is made"
	description="Where and how AI was used in building and writing Ramblings."
>
	<h1>How this is made</h1>

	<p>
		Ramblings is partly an experiment in building with AI agents, so it is worth being plain about where AI is
		used.
	</p>

	<h2>The site</h2>
	<p>
		The code is written by an AI coding agent (Claude Code). Every change goes through a pull request that I
		read and merge myself, and automated checks must pass before anything is published. The site is built with
		Astro and hosted on GitHub Pages. The
		<a href="https://github.com/NickJoyce-IO/ramblings">source is public</a>, including the history of how it
		was built.
	</p>

	<h2>The writing</h2>
	<p>
		The posts are written by me, from my own notes and experience. An AI agent may challenge an argument, point
		out weak spots or suggest edits, but it does not write the posts for me.
	</p>

	<h2>Views</h2>
	<p>These are my personal views and do not represent those of my employer.</p>
</BaseLayout>
